IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`
IMPORT `crtpa-s8-supplementary`
IMPORT `crtpa-s9-arbitration`

-- Tests for sections 8 and 9.  Every expected value is written from the text of ss 8 and 9, with the reason
-- beside it, before the module was run.  In each call the inputs are, in order, those of the rule's GIVEN.

§ `Tests -- s 8(1)`

#ASSERT `s 8(1) section 2 affects a right or remedy of the third party that exists or is available apart from this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(1) section 2 affects a right or remedy of the third party that exists or is available apart from this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 8(2)`

-- "does not apply where the negligence consists of the breach of an obligation arising from a term of a contract and the person seeking to enforce it is a third party acting in reliance on section 2."
#ASSERT `s 8(2) section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(2) section 2(2) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 does not apply` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 8(3)`

#ASSERT `s 8(3) the action is one founded on a contract for the purposes of section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the action is one founded on a contract for the purposes of section 6 of the Limitation Act 1959` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the period is the Limitation Act's, stated by the person (here, 6 years, a figure of this test and not of the Act).
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the period that applies to the action, in years` TRUE (JUST 6) EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the period that applies to the action, in years` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(3) the period that applies to the action, in years` FALSE (JUST 6) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 8(4)`

#ASSERT `s 8(4) the third party is treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law` `section 2(5)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the third party is treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law` `section 4(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the third party is treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law` `section 4(6)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the third party is treated as a party to the contract for the purposes of any other written law` `a provision other than section 2(5), 4(4) or 4(6)` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 9(1)`

-- inputs: the third party has a right under s 2 to enforce the substantive term; the right is subject to an arbitration term; which Act the agreement is in writing for; the dispute asked about.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE TRUE `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE TRUE `neither of those` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE FALSE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` FALSE TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another dispute is outside the treatment, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `any other dispute` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` FALSE FALSE `neither of those` `any other dispute` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "(as the case may be)": the Act in question is the one the agreement is in writing for.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` TRUE TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST `the Arbitration Act 2001`
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` TRUE TRUE `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS JUST `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994`
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` TRUE TRUE `neither of those` `a dispute between the third party and the promisor relating to the enforcement of the substantive term by the third party` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the Act for the purposes of which the third party is treated as a party` TRUE TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` `any other dispute` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 9(2)`

-- inputs: a right to enforce a term providing for arbitration; which Act the agreement is in writing for; the third party falls to be treated under (1); the third party exercises the right; the time asked about.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `immediately before the exercise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `earlier than immediately before the exercise` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `Part 2 of the International Arbitration Act 1994` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `neither of those` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` FALSE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST FALSE) TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): the third party already falls to be treated as a party under (1), so (2) is not the route.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST TRUE) TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "if the third party exercises the right".
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` (JUST FALSE) FALSE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` NOTHING FALSE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)'s answer not stated.
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the third party is treated as a party to the arbitration agreement` TRUE `the Arbitration Act 2001` NOTHING TRUE `at or after the exercise` EQUALS NOTHING
